{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-23T17:23:25.235Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"6fe7ba654eae068ba842efbc","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.330","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1773"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1773: refusal envelopes echo URL userinfo when it contains whitespace and a percent-encoded @ separator"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"GH-1773 (filed 2026-11-23 from the pm-rust parity review, reproduced on the pinned pm-cli oracle; native and TS behave the same). A refusal envelope echoes an open blocker's title verbatim. When that title holds a URL whose userinfo contains whitespace and a percent-encoded @ (https://fixture:fake words%40example.invalid/path), the userinfo is not masked: pm start-task sample-one --json refused by that blocker prints 'fixture:fake words'. Expected: credential-shaped URL userinfo is masked in every refusal and diagnostic projection, whitespace-bearing userinfo and an encoded separator included, matching the masking of plain user:pass@host; plain masking unchanged. Duplicate check: searched redaction URL userinfo whitespace percent-encoded separator refusal envelope; pm-gh1707 (closed) fixed public-URL @-in-path over-redaction and claim-refusal echoes, pm-nhauur and pm-5htunt (closed) cover other echo surfaces, none covers whitespace plus encoded separators."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","gh:1773","privacy","redaction","security"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-23T17:23:25.235Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-23T17:23:25.235Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":90},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"A redaction corpus case covers whitespace in userinfo with a percent-encoded separator, applied to refusal envelopes, diagnostics and JSON and TOON output; Plain user:pass@host masking and public URLs with @ in the path are unchanged"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-qwoy"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/reporter","value":"unbraind"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Credential-shaped URL userinfo is masked in refusals and diagnostics whatever whitespace or encoding it carries"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-gh1707","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-23T17:23:25.235Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"565a8229e32808e05336bdaefea6f1933279274465cadfe47900200a43f14a72","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"e582518bdcd0a7d96057c73acd54132ad51e580a4d510cccb5a28d85ea5056db"}
