{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-23T21:44:48.291Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"8236d322061fd32d87fda357","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1773","claim:pm-gh1775","lineage:pm-gh1773","lineage:pm-qwoy","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1773+pm-gh1775","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1773","claim:pm-gh1775","lineage:pm-gh1773","lineage:pm-qwoy","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.330","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-23T21:44:48.291Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-23T21:44:48.289Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Root cause and fix (2026-11-23): redactUrlCredentialsInText judged each whitespace-delimited word alone, so a stored title holding a URL whose password contains a blank split into a scheme word with a colon but no at sign and a host word with an at sign (or its percent escape) but no colon; neither word matched the token rule. The plain at-sign form leaked the same way, not only the encoded one, and Node's WHATWG URL parser reads that spelling as userinfo with a spaced password. Fix in src/core/shared/url-credentials.ts: before the word rule, a word with no at sign that opens a URL authority with a user-colon prefix (scheme, one or two slashes, a colon that port digits alone never follow, no path, no bracketed IPv6 host) is joined across any whitespace with the later words up to the first that holds an at sign or its escape, within 16 words and 512 code units and before another URL starts, and the joined span goes through redactUrlCredentialsInToken. Line breaks and tabs count as blanks because URL parsers drop them. Host-and-port and plain-host prose before a later at sign stays intact. Every outbound surface (refusal guidance in JSON and text, telemetry sanitizeString, Sentry scrubbing) already routes free text through this one function. Verified end to end in a sandbox: a start-task refusal gated by such a blocker now prints the scheme, the placeholder and the host only, in JSON and TOON output."}]}],"before_hash":"6c9e717a22c407c414b9d0c38ff6010eb30da0789b1976f47ae90d84cb199352","after_hash":"1855d8cbd165c4178371ca28261bc5ab1c572b8dc81c7779b17ceb187052328f","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"221f6626ce589eb2e137069dd2382d4e4134612fe7c7fa3f599937004fa5bd3c"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-23T22:40:06.040Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"8236d322061fd32d87fda357","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1773","claim:pm-gh1775","lineage:pm-gh1773","lineage:pm-qwoy","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1773+pm-gh1775","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1773","claim:pm-gh1775","lineage:pm-gh1773","lineage:pm-qwoy","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.330","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-23T22:40:06.039Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Rework after Codex review round 1 (2026-11-23, 8 URL findings). The opening word may now hold its own separator (an encoded at sign inside the password), skips any number of authority slashes, ignores a colon that only appears in a query or fragment, exempts only a real host:port head (a label run, a colon and at least one digit), and also opens on a single dotless label when a later word carries the user-password colon (a spaced username). The continuation takes the LAST at sign or its escape that starts within 16 words and 512 code units, as a URL parser takes the authority's last at sign; the word holding it may run past the length bound (a long query), and a word that starts another URL or holds a path delimiter before any separator ends the search. All 8 reproductions are pinned in tests/unit/core/shared/url-credentials.spec.ts, and the earlier prose and bound cases still pass."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-23T22:40:06.040Z"}],"before_hash":"1855d8cbd165c4178371ca28261bc5ab1c572b8dc81c7779b17ceb187052328f","after_hash":"da4d08059259ef3ed13b59f2e5d0fb8022c1f38cc35d546f915d3b4d9ea244cd","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"a2eb83a3fb6e21befad3e1903ce347e3b218aa758319b75fcec8d46215dc304f"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-23T22:56:20.810Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"8236d322061fd32d87fda357","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1773","claim:pm-gh1775","lineage:pm-gh1773","lineage:pm-qwoy","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1773+pm-gh1775","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1773","claim:pm-gh1775","lineage:pm-gh1773","lineage:pm-qwoy","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.330","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-23T22:56:20.809Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Codex review round 2 (2026-11-23): a redirect URL in the final word's query stopped the scan before its separator (now only a scheme at the end of the text before the first path delimiter starts another URL, read back from the colon, which also removes the quadratic unanchored scheme search Codex measured); a dotted spaced username and a password starting with digits were not joined (any colon-bearing head that is no dotted or localhost host:port now opens, and a dotless or dotted label opens when a later word carries a colon with text after it); a quoted URL followed by prose with a colon was over-redacted (a quote, backtick or angle bracket in the authority ends it). Declined with reason: preserving the host and path after a join — the single-token rule masks through the last at sign by design (GH-1707, base64 passwords hold slashes), and the joined span is pinned to redact exactly as the same URL without blanks."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-23T22:56:20.810Z"}],"before_hash":"da4d08059259ef3ed13b59f2e5d0fb8022c1f38cc35d546f915d3b4d9ea244cd","after_hash":"e0325bb4f4e84f911b991a0b0d345aa559854ca7a044cca427e2ce38ac5a765e","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"6c163f970e43e6fcac35c1ffacd0d5cf7e5d343746e38d9424acac1465dc8270"}
